                <pb facs="0140" n="42" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg42"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760c.60f/11: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wallace</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-06-15T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 15, 1920—6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1117. Your telegram 1279, June 12th, 6 P.M.</p>
                <p>This Government has no objection to decision of the conference of Ambassadors in
                    regard to the plan of arbitration to determine the attribution of the Duchy of
                    Teschen thus renouncing plebiscite provided governments of Poland and
                    Czechoslovakia agree. The Department has so informed Legations at Prague and
                    Warsaw.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
